    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass, including the new `Cp35Tests`. The change is complete.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe soft-match duplicate rule for `POST /api/owners`: a new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a different telephone is still created, and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is false and `possibleDuplicateOf` is absent.\n\nChanges, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n1. **New function step** `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 scans existing owners for one with the same `lastName` (case-insensitive), same `postcode`, and a different `telephone`, picking the lowest id when several match, and mutates the built `Owner` in place. It runs after `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (which already rejects hard 409 duplicates) so it's never confused with a hard duplicate, and before `SaveOwner` so the flags persist.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 added the `assignPossibleDuplicate` step to `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` between `ensureUniqueIdentity` and `assignHouseholdMemberCount`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\n3. **Owner entity** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (primitive `boolean`, defaults false so it's always present) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (nullable `Integer`) columns with accessors.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` and `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` to all four `schema.sql` variants (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres); h2 is the active profile.\n\n5. **OpenAPI** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them and MapStruct maps them by name for the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response the test reads back.",
